  "Metadata": {
    "Summary": "Runtime IK for s&box: two-bone limbs, look-at, foot placement, and FABRIK chains, zero setup.",
    "Description": "Better IK gives any skinned model working, stable runtime IK: TwoBoneIK (arms/legs with a proper pole vector), LookAtIK (clamped head/eye aim), FootPlacementIK (ground conformance and pelvis drop on top of TwoBoneIK), and FabrikIK (unconstrained variable-length chains for tails, tentacles, ropes) - all computed analytically every frame. Drop a component on the relevant bone; it walks the skeleton to find the chain automatically, works on Citizen or any custom rig, and layers on top of the animgraph instead of fighting it.\n\nSource & issues: https://github.com/zeljkovranjes/sbox-better-ik",
    "WebsiteUrl": "https://github.com/zeljkovranjes/sbox-better-ik"
  }
}
